# 🛠️ Local Setup

## Prerequisites

Install the following tools:

```text
Docker
Kind
kubectl
Helm
Git
GitHub Actions Self-hosted Runner
jq
bc
```

Verify installation:

```bash
docker --version

kind version

kubectl version --client

helm version

jq --version

bc --version
```

---

# 1️⃣ Create the Kind Cluster

Create the Kubernetes cluster:

```bash
kind create cluster \
  --config kind-config.yaml
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get nodes
```

Expected output:

```text
NAME                         STATUS   ROLES
agentic-cicd-control-plane   Ready    control-plane
```

---

# 2️⃣ Install Argo CD

Create the namespace:

```bash
kubectl create namespace argocd
```

Install Argo CD:

```bash
kubectl apply \
  -n argocd \
  -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/stable/manifests/install.yaml
```

Wait for the pods:

```bash
kubectl get pods -n argocd
```

---

# 3️⃣ Install OpenTelemetry Operator

Add the Helm repository:

```bash
helm repo add open-telemetry \
  https://open-telemetry.github.io/opentelemetry-helm-charts
```

Update repositories:

```bash
helm repo update
```

Install the Operator:

```bash
helm install opentelemetry-operator \
  open-telemetry/opentelemetry-operator \
  -n opentelemetry-operator-system \
  --create-namespace
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get pods \
  -n opentelemetry-operator-system
```

---

# 4️⃣ Configure Kubernetes RBAC

Apply the RBAC configuration:

```bash
kubectl apply \
  -f otel-rbac.yaml
```

---

# 5️⃣ Deploy the OpenTelemetry Collector

Deploy the Collector:

```bash
kubectl apply \
  -f otel-collector.yaml
```

Verify:

```bash
kubectl get pods
```

The collector should run as a DaemonSet.

---

# 6️⃣ Verify Metrics Collection

Check the collector logs:

```bash
kubectl logs \
  -n default \
  -l app.kubernetes.io/name=opentelemetry-collector
```

Metrics should eventually appear in Elastic.

---

# 7️⃣ Configure Elastic Cloud

Create an Elastic Cloud project.

The project provides:

```text
Elasticsearch
+
Kibana
+
Agent Builder
+
MCP Server
```

Configure the OpenTelemetry exporter with the appropriate Elastic endpoint and authentication credentials.

---

# 8️⃣ Create the ES|QL Health Check

Create an ES|QL query that:

1. Reads Kubernetes node metrics.
2. Aggregates node values.
3. Calculates memory usage.
4. Returns structured health information.

Conceptually:

```text
working_set

/

(working_set + available)

×

100
```

The query output should contain:

```text
Node Name

Memory Usage %

CPU Usage
```

---

# 9️⃣ Create the Agent Builder Tool

Create an Elastic Agent Builder Tool named:

```text
k8s_node_health_check
```

Attach the ES|QL query.

The tool should be independently testable.

Example:

```text
Run Kubernetes node health check
```

---

# 🔟 Create the Agent

Create an Agent Builder Agent:

```text
kubernetes_analysis_agent
```

Attach:

```text
k8s_node_health_check
```

The agent can now answer questions such as:

```text
Is the Kubernetes cluster healthy?
```

This agent is primarily used to validate the agentic workflow.

