# 🔐 Security Notes

Never commit credentials to the repository.

Do not commit:

```text
Docker Hub tokens

Elastic API keys

Elastic endpoints containing sensitive data

GitHub runner tokens
```

Use GitHub Secrets:

```text
DOCKERHUB_USERNAME

DOCKERHUB_TOKEN

ELASTIC_MCP_ENDPOINT

ELASTIC_MCP_API_KEY
```

Example:

```yaml
${{ secrets.ELASTIC_MCP_API_KEY }}
```

---

# 🧩 Why This Is Not Just a Toy Project

## 🚦 It Is a Real Deployment Gate

The deployment job has a hard dependency on the health-check job.

```text
Health Check Fails

↓

Deploy Job Never Runs
```

This behavior was tested with both:

* Forced successful health checks
* Forced failed health checks

---

## 🤖 It Uses Agent Infrastructure for Automation

The project does not simply create a chatbot.

Instead, it uses agent infrastructure as part of an engineering workflow.

```text
Agent Builder

↓

Tool

↓

MCP

↓

CI/CD Pipeline
```

---

## 🎯 It Separates AI Reasoning From Deterministic Automation

The Agent:

```text
Used for:

Analysis

Reasoning

Conversation
```

The Tool:

```text
Used for:

Structured Data

Deterministic Automation

CI/CD Decisions
```

This is an intentional engineering design decision.

---

## 🔄 It Implements a Complete GitOps Loop

The full system is:

```text
Kubernetes

↓

OpenTelemetry

↓

Elastic Cloud

↓

Elasticsearch

↓

ES|QL

↓

Agent Builder Tool

↓

MCP

↓

GitHub Actions

↓

Git Commit

↓

Argo CD

↓

Kubernetes Deployment
```

Each component was independently tested before integration.

---

# 🌟 Why Agentic CI/CD?

Traditional CI/CD pipelines usually evaluate:

```text
Source Code

↓

Build

↓

Tests

↓

Artifact
```

Modern infrastructure systems also need awareness of:

```text
Runtime Environment

Cluster Health

Resource Availability

Operational Context
```

Agentic systems can provide an interface between:

```text
Automation

+

Observability

+

Infrastructure
```

This project demonstrates one possible pattern:

> **Use live observability data to influence deployment decisions.**

---

# 🧠 Core Engineering Principle

The most important design principle in this project is:

> ## **AI can help understand infrastructure, but critical deployment decisions should rely on structured and deterministic outputs.**

Therefore:

```text
AI Agent

↓

Analysis and Exploration
```

while:

```text
Structured Tool

↓

Deterministic CI/CD Gate
```

The MCP layer allows these capabilities to be integrated into automation workflows.

